AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::borrow()
├── when market is paused
│   └── it should revert with IsPaused for PAUSE_TYPE
├── when market is frozen but not paused
│   └── it should revert with IsPaused for FROZEN_TYPE
├── given callback data is nonempty
│   ├── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketCallbacksUnsupported
│   ├── it should check onBehalf is creditAccount before rejecting callback data
│   ├── it should reject the data before Base input and sender authorization checks
│   ├── it should reject callback data before validating a zero receiver
│   └── it should never call a receiver callback even if authorization storage is manipulated
├── given invalid Credit account
│   ├── when onBehalf is not creditAccount
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketUnauthorizedAccount
│   └── when onBehalf is zero address
│       └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketUnauthorizedAccount
├── given invalid Base inputs
│   ├── when assets and shares are both zero
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when assets and shares are both nonzero
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when receiver is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInvalidInput
│   └── when caller is neither creditAccount nor its authorized delegate
│       └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketUnauthorized
├── given interest accrual
│   ├── it should accrue with the old debt before calculating the draw
│   ├── when IRM call fails
│   │   └── it should revert without changing debt or minting tokens
│   └── when accrued debt leaves insufficient credit capacity
│       └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInsufficientMarketLiquidity
├── given borrowing by assets
│   ├── it should round the opening fee up from requested assets
│   ├── it should charge at least one fee asset when a positive fee rounds up from a small draw
│   ├── it should add the opening fee to debt assets
│   ├── it should calculate borrow shares rounded up from gross debt assets
│   └── it should mint only the requested net assets to receiver
├── given borrowing by shares
│   ├── it should round opening fee shares up from requested shares
│   ├── it should charge at least one fee share when a positive fee rounds up from a small share draw
│   ├── it should add opening fee shares before calculating gross debt assets
│   ├── it should calculate gross debt assets rounded down from total shares
│   └── it should mint gross debt assets minus opening fee assets to receiver
├── given credit and collateral limits
│   ├── when gross post-accrual debt exceeds creditLimit
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInsufficientMarketLiquidity
│   ├── when gross post-accrual debt equals creditLimit
│   │   └── it should succeed if solvent
│   ├── given accumulated badDebtAssets
│   │   ├── it should reduce available capacity by the full accumulated bad debt
│   │   ├── when active debt plus bad debt equals creditLimit
│   │   │   └── it should succeed if solvent
│   │   └── when active debt plus bad debt exceeds creditLimit
│   │       ├── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInsufficientMarketLiquidity
│   │       └── it should roll back debt fee and borrow-token minting atomically
│   ├── given bad debt containing unclaimed opening fees and the actual DUSD implementation
│   │   ├── it should reserve capacity for both already minted DUSD and unclaimed fees
│   │   └── it should roll back DUSD balance supply and minter accounting when remaining capacity is exceeded
│   ├── when both credit capacity and solvency would fail
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInsufficientMarketLiquidity before querying the oracle
│   ├── when the oracle price is zero
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidOraclePrice
│   ├── when the oracle call reverts
│   │   └── it should propagate the failure atomically
│   ├── when debt exceeds collateral value multiplied by maxLtv
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketBorrowingTooMuch
│   ├── when debt equals collateral value multiplied by maxLtv after rounding
│   │   └── it should succeed
│   └── when creditAccount has no collateral
│       └── it should revert for every positive draw
├── given uint128 accounting boundaries
│   ├── when gross debt assets cannot fit in totalBorrowed assets
│   │   └── it should revert atomically
│   ├── when calculated borrow shares cannot fit in totalBorrowed or position shares
│   │   └── it should revert atomically
│   └── when opening fee cannot fit in claimableFeesAssets
│       └── it should revert atomically including token mint and debt updates
├── given borrow token minting
│   ├── when market lacks minter permission
│   │   └── it should revert atomically
│   ├── when token ceiling is insufficient
│   │   └── it should revert atomically
│   ├── when borrow token is paused or mint otherwise reverts
│   │   └── it should revert atomically
│   ├── when mint succeeds but the later oracle or solvency check fails
│   │   └── it should roll back receiver balance and token minter accounting
│   ├── when borrow token attempts reentrancy
│   │   └── it should reject reentrancy and revert atomically
│   └── when receiver is any nonzero address
│       └── it should mint net assets to that receiver
└── given a successful draw
    ├── when caller is creditAccount
    │   └── it should succeed
    ├── when caller is an authorized delegate of creditAccount
    │   └── it should succeed
    ├── when opening fee is zero
    │   └── it should leave claimableFeesAssets unchanged
    ├── when opening fee is nonzero
    │   ├── it should increase claimableFeesAssets by opening fee assets
    │   └── it should return zero fee supply shares
    ├── when opening fee equals MATH_PRECISION
    │   └── it should apply the full permitted fee using the same rounding rules
    ├── it should update totalBorrowed assets and shares and creditAccount borrowShares
    ├── it should not change totalSupply or supply shares
    ├── it should not change collateral accounting staked assets idle assets or rewards
    ├── it should add both newly accrued interest and opening fee to claimableFeesAssets
    ├── it should emit AccrueInterest before Borrow with net assets and fee values
    └── it should return gross debt assets borrow shares and opening fee assets
